  "notes": "{大豆|だいず} is one of the most important crops in Japanese food culture.\n\nCOMMON SOYBEAN PRODUCTS:\n- {豆腐|とうふ}: tofu\n- {味噌|みそ}: miso\n- {醤油|しょうゆ}: soy sauce\n- {納豆|なっとう}: fermented soybeans\n- {枝豆|えだまめ}: edamame (young soybeans)\n- {豆乳|とうにゅう}: soy milk\n\n{節分|せつぶん} (the day before the start of spring) involves throwing roasted {大豆|だいず} while saying {鬼|おに}は{外|そと}、{福|ふく}は{内|うち} (Demons out, good fortune in).",
